 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">◆</span>Species Data Assets<span class=\"meta\">PDA_CreatureSpecies</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "One parent class, with child classes for blocks specific to a species (boids for the shoal, segment chain and charge for the serpent). Fields are grouped by category, and the categories show up as-is in the Creature Tuner:": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Identity": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Visual": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Navigation": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Perception": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Temperament": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Distances": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Behaviour frequencies": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Signals": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">≡</span>One pipeline for scans and observations": "abyss/tdd/",
 "A <b>scan</b> is simply a research task whose observable is permanent (active while the creature is alive). Scans and behaviour observations share <b>one pipeline</b>: there is no separate scan system.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Each task row holds its observable tag, required duration, max range and angle, prerequisites, the zone it unlocks, and hints that get more precise over time.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Gameplay Tags vs Enums": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Tags</b> for open sets that Designers extend: behaviours, observables, stimuli, zones.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Enums</b> for closed, ordered sets used in Switches: the vigilance stages (Calm, Suspicious, Warning, Aggressive) and the task states (Locked, Active, Completed).": "abyss/tdd/",
 "04 · Creature AI": "abyss/tdd/",
 "3D navigation without NavMesh, in three layers": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Unreal’s NavMesh only covers walkable surfaces, so creatures navigate in three layers, following Reynolds’ model (action selection, then path selection, then locomotion). It continues my <a href=\"../../flying-ai/\">Flying AI</a> project.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">⇢</span>Three layers<span class=\"meta\">Brains set goals · the component moves</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "1 · Decision": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Behavior Tree or State Tree. <em>What do I do?</em> Patrol, flee, hunt… gives a goal.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "2 · Route": "abyss/tdd/",
 "EQS query. <em>Where is my next free waypoint toward that goal?</em>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "3 · Locomotion": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Steering component + Floating Pawn Movement. <em>How do I swim there smoothly?</em>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Feelers alone are short-sighted and get stuck in U-shaped rocks. EQS alone zigzags and stops at each waypoint. EQS plans ahead; steering makes it look alive.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">⌖</span>Layer 2: EQS route<span class=\"meta\">Cheap tests first</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Distance to the creature</b>: a filter, kept as a ring between a min and a max distance.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Trace from the creature</b>: a filter, with a sphere as wide as the creature plus a margin.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Distance to the goal</b>: a score, closer is better.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Dot with the current velocity</b>: a score that rewards <b>continuity</b>, for smooth curves.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The distance filter runs first, so fewer points need a trace. All values come from the species data.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">≋</span>Layer 3: locomotion, every tick": "abyss/tdd/",
 "AI Perception (Sight and Hearing) is set to generous maximum values, and <b>each species’ perception is filtered in Blueprint</b> from its data. Why: sense settings can’t be changed at runtime from Blueprint, but the Creature Tuner must change perception live. The player’s sprint is a noise event; the flash is sent directly through an interface, since light is not a perception sense.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">✦</span>Fish shoal<span class=\"meta\">State Tree</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>One actor, 30 fish as instances</b> of one mesh, without collision. The actor is the anchor: it wanders with the steering component, and the fish follow it with boids rules (cohesion, alignment, separation, anchor pull), updated at 30 Hz in one batch per frame.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Shoal states": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Cruise": "abyss/tdd/",
