 "Always observable": "abyss/tdd/",
 "A charge that hits pushes the player back, shakes the camera and locks input for 1 s. <b>No death:</b> the punishment is losing position and time, which keeps the demo patient-friendly. Three ways to deter it, without a weapon: flash it, stay out of its territory, or sprint away. A Warning always comes before a Charge.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span class=\"n\">+</span>One system, two scales<span class=\"meta\">Target tier</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Abyssal Presence": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Not a real AI: a <mark class=\"hl\">scripted pass</mark> along a spline, in the dark beyond the flashlight, lit only by a few bioluminescent lights. It reuses the serpent’s segment chain at giant scale. Showing that one system serves both a 6 m serpent and a 150 m leviathan is a deliberate point.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Readable signals": "abyss/tdd/",
 "A signals component maps each observable to a light (colour, intensity, pulse) and a sound, from the species data. A Designer can change how a behaviour <mark class=\"hl\">announces itself</mark> from the Creature Tuner, without code.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "05 · Observation system": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">◉</span>Flow<span class=\"meta\">Checked every 0.1 s</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Creature brain": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Starts a behaviour and declares it observable, e.g. the serpent’s Warning.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Registry": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Keeps the short list of events active right now, in the Game State.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Tracker": "abyss/tdd/",
 "While the player holds observation mode: range, angle, line of sight, then progress builds up.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Research journal": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Completes the task, unlocks zones, tells the HUD.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">?</span>Why a registry": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The tracker only goes through events that are <b>active right now</b> (usually 1 to 5), instead of searching every actor every 0.1 s, or using an overlap that ignores what is actually observable. Emitters push, the tracker pulls a short list. It lives on the Game State because subsystems would need C++.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">♥</span>Forgiving by design": "abyss/tdd/",
 "If the target is lost, a <b>0.5 s grace time</b>, then progress <b>decays slowly</b>: never an instant reset. Tutorial values are generous (25° angle, 2 s).": "abyss/tdd/",
