 "07 · Creature Tuner": "abyss/tdd/",
 "A Designer picks a species, tunes it, spawns it and watches its perception, vigilance and observable events live, <b>without code</b>. It is the centrepiece of the demo video.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">⚒</span>Features<span class=\"meta\">Editor Utility Widget</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Species picker</b> from the Asset Registry, child classes included.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Edit values</b> in a Details View bound to the Data Asset: a new field added to the species class shows up on its own.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>New species</b> by duplicating an existing one, then changing mesh and values.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Spawn in play</b> in front of the camera, and <b>apply live</b> to every creature of that species.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Live monitor</b>: the selected creature’s behaviour, vigilance, perceived actors and speed, about 5 times per second.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Debug layers</b>: perception cone, vigilance bar, trajectory, EQS waypoints, safety trace, goal, active observables.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">⇄</span>Editor ↔ play session": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The widget lives in the <b>editor world</b>, the creatures in the <b>play world</b>. Assets are shared by both, so a <b>Data Asset serves as the channel</b>:": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Creature Tuner<small>editor world</small>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "transient bridge reference": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Bridge actor<small>play world · non-shipping</small>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The bridge registers itself in the channel when play starts and clears it when play ends. The reference is never saved: if it’s empty, the widget shows “Start PIE to spawn”. The same sharing explains live tuning: the creature in play reads the very asset the Details View edits.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span class=\"n\">▶</span>Video scenario<span class=\"meta\">Target</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Zero code": "abyss/tdd/",
 "A Designer duplicates the curious creature, renames it <em>Glimmer Ray</em>, swaps the mesh, makes it shyer (fear rises faster, larger inspect distance) and gives its inspect signal a yellow light. They spawn it in play and watch its fear bar and signals react to the player.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "08 · Debug tools &amp; risks": "abyss/tdd/",
 "On demand, each creature draws its perception cone (species values), vigilance bar and stage, trajectory, current and next EQS waypoints, safety trace (green if free, red if hit), goal and active observables. The Gameplay Debugger covers Behavior Trees, perception and EQS; the Visual Logger replays a charge after the fact. Debug drawing is off in shipping builds.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Main risks": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Risk": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Mitigation": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Blueprint cost of 30 boids (≈ 435 neighbour pairs per update)": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Frame drops": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Fixed 30 Hz update, batched instance updates, a third of the fish per frame, profiling with Unreal Insights. The <b>only valid case for C++</b>, proposed only if measurements exceed the budget.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Perception settings not editable at runtime from Blueprint": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The Tuner can’t tune perception": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Max values in the config, filtered in Blueprint from the species data.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Editor ↔ play communication for the Tuner": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Centrepiece blocked": "abyss/tdd/",
 "An early spike, and the shared-asset bridge. Fallback: tune in the editor, spawn with a debug key.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "State Tree learning curve, API changes": "abyss/tdd/",
